Project type: Hands-on Salesforce Administration & Platform App Builder Project
Methodology: Sprint-based delivery
Environment: Salesforce Developer Edition
1. Business Context
A housing counseling agency needs a centralized Salesforce application where housing counselors can manage their work while supervisors have appropriate access to oversee operations. Without a clearly structured application and defined access permissions, staff may have difficulty navigating the system, and sensitive information may not be accessible according to their responsibilities.
2. Business Requirements
The application needed to:
•	Provide a dedicated Salesforce app for HHCA's housing counseling operations.
•	Establish a role hierarchy representing the supervisor and counselor positions.
•	Create counselor and supervisor user accounts for testing different access levels.
•	Apply permission sets to grant access based on each user's responsibilities.
•	Validate that the configured access supports the intended operational needs.
3. What I Built
•	Custom Salesforce application: Created the HHCA application with counselor-facing navigation and relevant workspace tabs.
•	Role hierarchy: Established the HHCA organizational structure, with the HHCA Housing Counseling Supervisor above the HHCA Housing Counselor.
•	Test users: Created counselor and supervisor users to validate the configuration under different user contexts.
•	Permission sets: Created and assigned HHCA Counselor Access and HHCA Supervisor Access to support role-specific access requirements.
•	Access validation: Tested user access to relevant records and functionality to identify configuration gaps.
4. Scope and Out of Scope
In scope
•	Salesforce app creation and navigation.
•	Role hierarchy configuration.
•	Counselor and supervisor user setup.
•	Permission-set assignment and access validation.
•	Initial testing of role-specific access.
Out of scope
•	Lead intake and follow-up automation.
•	Advanced assignment logic and workflow automation.
•	Comprehensive reporting and dashboard development.
•	Production deployment and organization-wide rollout.
These items are reserved for subsequent milestones or future enhancements.
5. Testing and Results
I tested the configuration using the counselor and supervisor user contexts to validate access to the application and relevant functionality.
The supervisor user successfully accessed Leads, including counselor-owned Leads, accessed Tasks, and edited Counselor Profile records. These checks provided evidence that the configured access supported key supervisory activities.
The supervisor's Home page still required further refinement to provide useful information. That usability improvement was identified separately rather than treating the entire application experience as complete.
6. Business Value
This milestone established the foundation for a role-based housing counseling application. It created the organizational structure, user contexts, and permission framework needed to build subsequent lead management, follow-up automation, and reporting capabilities.
It also established a repeatable approach to validating Salesforce configuration before introducing more complex business processes.
7. Project Management Approach
I organized the work as a defined sprint with explicit requirements, scope boundaries, configuration deliverables, and validation activities. I separated future enhancements from the current deliverable to maintain focus and support incremental development.
